# Phase 8B.1 event-evaluation harness: event_eval_results.json is a fully
# deterministic, trivially-regeneratable output of a fixture-only run (no
# Gemini call, no extractor yet) — see dataset/event_eval/README.md's
# "Results file" section for the full rationale. Unlike
# dataset/scripts/benchmark_results*.json (real Gemini output, tracked
# deliberately as a comparison baseline), this file carries no unique
# information beyond what test_scorer.py already asserts precisely.
dataset/event_eval/event_eval_results.json

# Phase 8B.2 production evaluation adapter (run_production_eval.py):
# production_eval_results.json is this run's own generated output — real
# Gemini output, but produced by a one-off local evaluation run against
# throwaway projects, not yet adopted as a tracked comparison baseline.
# Left untracked for now, consistent with the event_eval_results.json
# policy above, until there's a specific, documented decision to track a
# given run as the reference baseline (the README's own "Results file"
# section anticipates this as a future possibility, not a default).
dataset/event_eval/production_eval_results.json

